# Testing Required

- Every new feature, bug fix, or behavior change must ship with Jest tests in `tests/`.
- Prefer extracting decision logic into `core.js` (pure functions, no `browser.*` calls) so it's directly unit-testable; don't bury business logic only inside `background.js` or UI scripts where it can't be tested without a browser.
- Before considering any change done, run both and require 0 failures / 0 lint errors:
  ```bash
  npm test
  npm run lint
  ```
- Extend existing `describe` blocks in `tests/core.test.js` or add new test files — don't skip coverage because a change seems "small".
- If something genuinely can't be unit tested (e.g. pure UI wiring in popup/options), say so explicitly instead of silently leaving it untested.
- CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs the same checks on every push/PR — a change isn't mergeable to `develop` if CI is red.
